SUMMARY:Graviera Festival\, Anopoli Sfakion
LOCATION:Anopoli\, Crete (Chania)\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:On the evening of 15 August the Anopoli cultural association and the Municipality of Sfakia lay a communal table on the plateau above Chora Sfakion: boiled meat with pilafi\, Sfakian stew\, graviera\, honey and wine\, with a Cretan kompania and the local dance society. It has run since the mid-1980s and draws people from all over Crete. Start is around 9 pm\; drive up the hairpins from Chora Sfakion in daylight and park on the plateau road.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/chania/#anopoli-graviera-festival-anopoli-sfakion
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/chania/#anopoli-graviera-festival-anopoli-sfakion
